 "inference": [
  "For three mines, stored blast damage times the grid value for the explosion's material against target 119 equals EA's stated damage against tanks: 150 x 2 = 300 (EOD Bot mine), 195 x 2 = 390 (M15, registry default), 160 x 3 = 480 (PTKM-1R). The PTKM-1R uses a different material and a different grid value, so it is an independent match.",
  "Field_674633de therefore behaves as a damage multiplier for that material pair. This is a correspondence with official numbers on three items, not a proof of the game's operation.",
  "For the M15 the product matches only with the registry default 195; the asset's own 300 would give 600. This strengthens L3320 and the registry rule of L3318."
 ],
 "unresolved": [
  "Target 119 is taken from L3205 as the tank material; it is not named in stored data. Test: one M15 under a main battle tank and one under an infantry fighting vehicle; equal readings of 390 would mean both use the same target material.",
  "The rule is checked on blast damage only. Test: one RPG hit square on a tank's side at close range, to compare with registry Damage 125 times the grid value 2 and the side angle curve of L3201.",
  "The SLAM's projectile cell reads 0.4375 and its explosion cells 0 and 1; EA's 199 to 363 is not reproduced. Test: SLAM hits on the side, front and underside of a full-health tank on the current build.",
  "No reading on the current build. Test: one PTKM-1R full hit on a full-health tank should read 480."
 ],
